        matching the web template literal exactly). Verified against internal/api/router.go:3316
        r.Get("/analytics/anomalies", anomalyHandler.GetAnomalies).
        Cache-then-network (ADR-013): the JsonElement envelope ({anomalies, health_summary,
        signals_monitored, anomalies_last_7d, anomalies_last_24h}) is cached under key "{vehicleId}:{days}"
        in CacheDomain.Anomalies, emitting cache slot (Loading) then refreshed network value (Success).
        TTL = CacheDomain.Anomalies 5.minutes == web STALE_TIMES.SLOW (5 * 60_000 ms) — verified in
        web/src/lib/constants.ts:48-60. The web queryKey ['anomalies', vehicleId, days] maps onto the
        per-(vehicle,window) feed identity in the store (one shared upstream per (vehicleId, days) tuple).
        enabled: vehicleId !== null reproduced as the disabled-feed gate: a null vehicleId returns a
        stable shared feed that never touches the repository and stays at the initial Loading slot
        (asserted: disabledFeedNeverFetchesAndStaysLoading, refreshIsNoOpForADisabledFeed).

Mutations (0): the web hook file contains exactly one useQuery and no mutations, so there is no
invalidation surface — neither the S7 port nor the S8 holder exposes a write/refresh-all path.
refreshAnomalies(vehicleId, days) re-collects an OBSERVED feed (asserted:
refreshReFetchesTheObservedFeed); it is a no-op for an unobserved or disabled feed (asserted:
refreshIsNoOpForAnUnobservedFeed, refreshIsNoOpForADisabledFeed).

